This repository contains original work plus patches against two upstream
projects. Neither project's source code is redistributed here;
scripts/setup.sh fetches both from their canonical repositories at pinned
revisions.

  colibrì — https://github.com/JustVugg/colibri
  Copyright the colibrì authors, Apache License 2.0.
  Its C engine, GPU backend header, and GPU conformance suite are fetched at
  build time. Two mechanical edits are applied by scripts/setup.sh: the
  entry points of c/colibri.c and c/tests/test_backend_cuda.cu are renamed so
  that a Zig main can call them, and c/uring.h's Linux guard is widened with
  __has_include so the file compiles against sysroots that lack the kernel
  UAPI headers. patches/ holds two further changes, both described in README.md.

  ZML — https://github.com/zml/zml
  Copyright the ZML authors, Apache License 2.0.
  Fetched at build time and patched to support sub-byte (u4/u2) device buffer
  transfers; see patches/zml-pjrt-subbyte-transfer.patch.

The quantization formats implemented in coli/backend.zig follow the codecs
defined in colibrì's c/quant.h, which is the normative definition of its
on-disk weight encodings.
